From 0622a4a4c2207221bb45e1bda6a26313676f7c07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cohost u3 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:02:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 15b-17: internal reduce per collection; integer_range and
 vector seqs chunk; chunked walks; chunk_next shares its buffer

Draft: doc/upstream/jank-15-reduce-walk.md (part two) and jank-17-range-chunks.md in
johnmn3/cohost.cljc. Applies after 11, 13, 14, 18, 19 (max/main) and 15a-16-in-place-walks.patch; it uses 11-sorted-walk's shared-buffer array_chunk (no array_chunk change of its own). Repros: bash
dev/research/upstream/run.sh 17-range-chunks (Expected: chunked-seq? true for
(seq (range 10)) and a vector seq; the lazy pipeline near the chunked loop) and
run.sh 15-reduce-walk (reduce + v near the nth loop).

- runtime::reduce: a visit_object dispatch with direct loops, as reduce_kv has:
  persistent_vector and persistent_vector_sequence over immer's leaves
  (for_each_chunk_p), persistent_list over its data, the three persistent maps
  over their pairs (map entries as the map seq makes them), integer_range over
  its count; a lazy seq is realized and its inner seq dispatched; a chunked seq
  (chunked_cons, range) is reduced a chunk at a time and its chunked_next
  dispatched again; anything else takes the in-place walk. reduced stops every loop.
- integer_range: chunked_first (an array_chunk of up to 32 boxed values, made per
  call: no state, no mutex) and chunked_next, so chunked-seq? is true and
  core.jank's map/filter/doseq chunk branches fire.
- persistent_vector_sequence: chunked_first copies the rest of the immer leaf at the
  index (at most 32 refs) into a chunk, chunked_next is the seq after that leaf.
- sequence_range: the walk reads a chunked_cons through its array_chunk's buffer
  (no allocation per element), then goes on to its tail; iterator::rest() gives
  the rest as a seq mid-chunk (apply_to's rest args, skip()).
- chunk-cons keeps its rest unrealized (Clojure's ChunkedCons keeps `more`);
  chunked_cons::next and its in-place step realize the tail when they step past
  the chunk, and chunk_next returns a seq. Before, chunk_cons called seq(rest),
  so a chunked lazy pipeline realized its whole chain recursively: (count (map
  inc (range 0.0 1000000.0))) segfaults on the unpatched tree, and with
  integer_range chunked (count (map inc (range 1e6))) did too.
- chunked_cons::first reads an array_chunk head directly.

